# CLASS-C CUTOVER-ELIGIBLE READ ROUTES ONLY.
# Every path here is a read-only Node shadow that passed live Python↔Node
# parity and whose Python GET handler performs no GET-time business write.
# A future traffic cutover may route ONLY these paths to Node.
#
# One `/api/...` route path per line, EXACTLY as registered inside
# `backend-node/src/**` (Fastify path syntax, e.g. `:pid` not `{pid}`).
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Routes that are registered in src/ but are NOT cutover-eligible (deferred
# write-on-GET shadows, parked writers, precedence guards) live in
# `.migration-deferred`. A path must never appear in both files.
#
# Adding a route here without an accompanying implementation + tests +
# gate authorisation is NOT permitted. Removing a route requires an
# explicit rollback gate (Gate 7t removed 6a–6d and the Gate-4/5 writers).
